\section{Search an Issue Packet without Leaking Reservations}

Greedy selection within a cycle can pick an operation that blocks a
better packet. For a toy two-wide target, suppose every candidate
is individually ready at the current cycle, all dependence distances
are positive, and the ready set contains no terminator. Some operations
use only one pipeline, others need two pipelines at once. Let each
candidate have a positive priority representing scheduling urgency.
The packet builder below returns the locally highest sum of priorities,
not a globally optimal schedule. It runs against a snapshot of the
resource state, including future reservations made in earlier cycles.

\begin{sudocode}[Enumerate the packets for one issue cycle]
\State $best\gets []$; $score\gets 0$
\ForAll{ordered packets $p$ of one or two distinct ready ops}
  \State $trial\gets$ copy of current reservation state
  \ForAll{$i$ in $p$ in order}
    \If{\Call{Issue}{$trial,i$} fails}
      \State skip this $p$ \Comment{Discard partial reservations}
    \EndIf
  \EndFor
  \If{$\sum_{i\in p} priority[i]>score$}
    \State remember $p$, its score and $trial$
  \EndIf
\EndFor
\State install remembered state if nonempty
  \Comment{One chosen packet commits}
\State \Return $best$
\end{sudocode}

For two free pipelines $A,B$, take $X$ needing both with priority 7,
$Y$ needing only $A$ with priority 5, and $Z$ needing only $B$ with
priority 4. A highest-first scheduler issues $X$ alone. The builder
returns $[Y,Z]$ or $[Z,Y]$ with score 9. Make $B$ busy for this
cycle as a second test: now even $X$ alone cannot issue, and the
packet is $[Y]$ with score 5. When testing an $X$ candidate that
checks $A$ before $B$, require the failed trial not to consume $A$.

The invariant is that the selected reservation state results from
replaying exactly the chosen packet from the original snapshot.
Enumeration costs $O(R^2)$ trials at width two for $R$ ready
operations, and becomes expensive at larger widths. Limiting the
candidate set can save time, but then the score is only best among
those examined. Measure makespan separately: packing a cycle well
can still delay a critical chain.
